  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The expression \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\left(\\frac{(x+1)^2(x^2-x+1)^2}{(x^3+1)^2}\\right)^2\\\\ &\\quad{}\\cdot \\left(\\frac{(x-1)^2(x^2+x+1)^2}{(x^3-1)^2}\\right)^2 \\end{aligned} \\] equals:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\((x+1)^4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\((x^3+1)^4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\big[(x^3+1)(x^3-1)\\big]^2\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\big[(x^3-1)^2\\big]^2\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "1"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1951-p40.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\[ \\begin{aligned} x^3+1&=(x+1)(x^2-x+1),\\\\ x^3-1&=(x-1)(x^2+x+1), \\end{aligned} \\] each fraction inside parentheses equals \\(1\\) wherever the original expression is defined. Their squared product is therefore \\(1.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(x^3+1\\) and \\(x^3-1\\)",
        "Use \\(x^3+1=(x+1)(x^2-x+1)\\) and the analogous difference formula"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
